# Reusable Components First

Never write UI or business logic "openly" in pages, App, or one-off files.

## Must

- **UI primitives come from shadcn/ui** in `src/components/ui/`. Add with `npx shadcn@latest add <name>`, then customize the generated source in place (do not wrap third-party npm UI kits).
- Shared composites (Header, EmptyState, PageLayout, **Loading**) go in `components/common`.
- Loading states must use `Loading` / `LoadingScreen` / `LoadingOverlay` (chatbot SVG) — never ad-hoc spinners.
- Feature-only UI goes in `features/<name>/components/`.
- Pages and features **compose** components; they do not duplicate JSX patterns.
- Extract repeated markup, handlers, or fetch logic into components, hooks, or services.
- Prefer extending/modifying an existing shadcn component over inventing a parallel primitive.

## Do Not

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — loose markup in App or page
function App() {
  return (
    <div>
      <button className="px-4 py-2 bg-blue-500" onClick={...}>Save</button>
      {/* duplicated forms, cards, tables inline */}
    </div>
  );
}
```

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — compose reusable components
function UsersPage() {
  return (
    <PageLayout title="Users">
      <UserTable users={users} onEdit={handleEdit} />
      <Button variant="primary" onClick={handleCreate}>Add user</Button>
    </PageLayout>
  );
}
```

## When user drifts

If the user asks for quick inline junk that should be a component, **explain** that we extract a reusable component first, then use it — then implement that way.
